    "created_at": "2025-02-26T15:07:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-26T15:07:27Z",
    "body": "There might be interaction between the default state of the DTR/RTS signals and your board's circuitry for resetting the ESP32 into the bootloader. If you haven't already seen it, Espressif's reference designs usually incorporate some extra auto-reset circuitry that guards against the board being held in reset by a program naively treating the serial port flow control pins as flow control pins:\nhttps://docs.espressif.com/projects/esptool/en/latest/esp32/advanced-topics/boot-mode-selection.html#automatic-bootloader\n\nYou may need to play with the DTR/RTS settings after opening the port through webserial to find something that works reliably with your specific design.",
